                                                "text": "Sometimes her prose hyperventilates (\"Once, years ago, his and N.'s love for each other had glowed like phosphorescent fire on the surfaces of their bodies\"), and she has a weakness for epiphanies (\"There was a man, no longer young, though not yet old, who, traveling alone in northern Europe, began to feel that his soul was being drained slowly, almost secretly from him, drop by drop\")."
